  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-llm-workbuddy-cn",
      "text": "**English** | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nA [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) (`dsh`) plugin for **Tencent WorkBuddy**.\n\nSign in through your browser — **no API key required** — and use WorkBuddy's own model list."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **Browser OAuth sign-in** — authorize in a normal browser tab; no API key needed, ever. Sign in to either the China or the international site.\n- **Full model catalog** — WorkBuddy's own models, with context windows, output caps, and credit multipliers; server-side additions and removals are picked up automatically.\n- **Streaming chat** — responses stream in real time.\n- **Tool calls** — function calling, with a clear error when a model does not support it.\n- **Reasoning effort** — pick a thinking level for models that support one.\n- **Image input** — attach images for vision-capable models (models without vision support may be routed to a different model by the server).\n- **Usage indicator** — a quota bar in the Web UI sidebar for both personal and enterprise plans, with an optional custom cap and a configurable danger threshold."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "| Requirement | Version |\n| --- | --- |\n| DeepSeek Harness (`dsh`) | `>= 0.1.7-rc.1` |\n\nWeb UI features such as the settings page, model picker, and usage indicator require the `web` profile."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Add the plugin to a dsh profile — the `web` profile backs the Web UI:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:wenh56884-wq/dsh-llm-workbuddy\n```\n\nThe repository ships its compiled `lib/`, so a Git install needs no build step and no\ndev dependencies. Installing from a source checkout works too:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add /path/to/dsh-llm-workbuddy\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Sign in",
      "text": "Open **Settings → WorkBuddy** in the Web UI and pick a site: **Sign in (China)** for [www.workbuddy.cn](https://www.workbuddy.cn) or **Sign in (Intl)** for [www.workbuddy.ai](https://www.workbuddy.ai). The browser login opens in a new tab; the harness writes the credential automatically. No terminal needed."
    },
    {
      "section": "Sign in",
      "text": "The two sites are the same service on different hosts but hold **separate accounts** — one site's account does not work on the other — so the site is chosen per sign-in and recorded with the credential. Every later request goes to the host that issued it. To move to the other site, sign out and sign in again.\n\nAlternatively, sign in from the terminal:\n\n```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "Sign in to the China site (the default; equivalent to --site cn)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web exec dsh-workbuddy-login"
    },
    {
      "section": "Sign in to the international site",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web exec dsh-workbuddy-login --site intl"
    },
    {
      "section": "Show the signed-in account, its site, and the model list",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web exec dsh-workbuddy-login --status"
    },
    {
      "section": "Remove the stored credential",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web exec dsh-workbuddy-login --logout\n```\n\nOnce signed in, WorkBuddy's models appear in the model picker."
    },
    {
      "section": "Build",
      "text": "From a source checkout:\n\n```bash\npnpm install\npnpm run build\n```\n\nThis compiles the host half with `tsc` and bundles the Web client half with `esbuild`, both into `lib/`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Provenance and license",
      "text": "MIT. This plugin is a WorkBuddy adaptation of\n[`@shatyuka/dsh-llm-codebuddy`](https://github.com/shatyuka/dsh-llm-codebuddy)\n(MIT, © 2026 Shatyuka), which is the original work it derives from: the host\narchitecture, the browser-OAuth handshake, the model-catalog reader, the\nsettings page, and the usage indicator are all its author's design. This\nrepository re-points that client at the WorkBuddy deployments — the site list,\nthe product token every request identifies itself as, and the provider,\nsettings, and credential identifiers are WorkBuddy's — and renames it\naccordingly. The upstream copyright notice is retained in\n[`LICENSE`](./LICENSE) as the license requires."
    },
    {
      "section": "Provenance and license",
      "text": "When the upstream project releases fixes, they can be diffed in against this\ntree: the changes here are confined to the identifiers, the two service roots\nin `src/constants.ts`, and the catalogue User-Agent documented there."
    }
  ],
